MID_EV11_063_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_063_m01_001: Cai. Perfect timing.
MID_EV11_063_m01_002: What do you mean?
MID_EV11_063_m01_003: Aurora's spirits are low. I'm hoping you wouldn't\nmind talking to her.
MID_EV11_063_m01_004: I'm not sure if she's feeling more sad or...distracted.
MID_EV11_063_m01_005: Cai, good. I need you to hear me out. I've had some\ntroubling things on my mind for quite some time.
MID_EV11_063_m01_006: The thing is, I've been running away from my issues \nwith my father for such a long time now.
MID_EV11_063_m01_032: I blamed him when my mother was executed, and I\ncouldn't bring myself to forgive him.
MID_EV11_063_m01_033: I was convinced that my mother died because he\ncouldn't—or wouldn't—protect her.
MID_EV11_063_m01_034: I could never come to terms with her death.
MID_EV11_063_m01_035: I was sad and resentful, my mind in chaos.
MID_EV11_063_m01_036: I pushed my father aside and hid myself away in\nmy temple.
MID_EV11_063_m01_037: When I was ordered into seclusion because of the\ndisappearances, I was fine with it at the time.
MID_EV11_063_m01_038: In my solitude, I've considered a great many\nmysteries about myself.
MID_EV11_063_m01_039: I thought about whose child I am, and I've\nwondered what my father thinks about all this.
MID_EV11_063_m01_040: The thought of facing questions to which I might not\nwant to know the answers nearly crushed me.
MID_EV11_063_m01_041: But among my thoughts swirled my utmost dread:\nseeing my father.
MID_EV11_063_m01_042: It was Castor who led me out of that dark place.
MID_EV11_063_m01_043: Despite everything, I couldn't help but wonder if my\nfather got the worst of our misfortunes.
MID_EV11_063_m01_044: Tucked safely behind these walls, I now realize I've\njust been hiding.
MID_EV11_063_m01_007: And here you are, Cai, fighting so hard for Castor.
MID_EV11_063_m01_008: You're so different from me. I'm frozen, in fear of\ntaking any action.
MID_EV11_063_m01_009: And yet, even if you can save him, your father's\nfuture is uncertain.
MID_EV11_063_m01_010: Mom, think about ol' Morrow's situation. He didn't\nsee things in such a negative way.
MID_EV11_063_m01_011: His family was trapped in that painting for so long,\nbut he's focused on the time he has left with them.
MID_EV11_063_m01_030: He inspires me. And he should inspire you too.
MID_EV11_063_m01_031: Worrying about how little time we have won't buy us\nmore of it. Let's make the most of our lives with Pop.
MID_EV11_063_m01_012: Yes... You're right.
MID_EV11_063_m01_013: Thank you, Cai.
MID_EV11_063_m01_014: I've allowed my circumstances to keep me from\naction for such a long time now.
MID_EV11_063_m01_015: While I remain here, I can make everything Father's\nfault. But there's more to the story than that.
MID_EV11_063_m01_016: Nothing stays the same forever. Look at you. You've\ngrown into a fine young man.
MID_EV11_063_m01_017: And here I am with more time than most, yet I'm\nthe one who refuses to change.
MID_EV11_063_m01_018: When I see you giving everything you have to help\nthose around you, it brings me courage.
MID_EV11_063_m01_019: I want us to be together as a family too, for\nhowever long that may last.
MID_EV11_063_m01_020: What's important is that we make as many precious\nmemories as we can.
MID_EV11_063_m01_021: And I want to take care of Castor until his\nfinal breath.
MID_EV11_063_m01_022: After all, he is my beloved husband.
MID_EV11_063_m01_023: Cai, I'm going to speak with Father.
MID_EV11_063_m01_024: I am feeling like I want to storm in and give him\na piece of my mind right now.
MID_EV11_063_m01_025: Hold on, Mom. Let's not get ahead of ourselves.
MID_EV11_063_m01_026: Let me win the games, and I'll bring you to Solel.
MID_EV11_063_m01_027: You're right again. Thank you, Cai.
MID_EV11_063_m01_028: Cai, speaking of the games, it seems the details for\nthe final round have been announced.
MID_EV11_063_m01_029: We'll need to do everything we can to prepare for\nour opponent, the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV11_064_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_064_m01_001: It's your final fight, Cai.
MID_EV11_064_m01_002: Mom, Centurio, I'm glad you're both here.
MID_EV11_064_m01_003: We'll be watching you from the stands, so do your\nbest. But don't try anything too risky, got it?
MID_EV11_064_m01_004: I'll be saying my prayers to the progenitor god, even\nthough I've never met her myself.
MID_EV11_064_m01_005: I'll ask that everything goes well and that you're\nreturned to me safely.
MID_EV11_064_m01_006: Everyone, before we head into the fight, I want to\nsay something.
MID_EV11_064_m01_007: Tialla, Peter, Ultand, I couldn't have made it this far\nwithout you.
MID_EV11_064_m01_008: And we've had a lot of good people supporting us\nalong the way.
MID_EV11_064_m01_009: To be honest, though, when we started, I thought we\nwere probably a long shot, at best.
MID_EV11_064_m01_010: But here we are, one win away from making my\nwish come true.
MID_EV11_064_m01_011: Bertrand is very strong, and I'm not sure we can\nbeat him.
MID_EV11_064_m01_012: But I'm asking, one more time, please help me do\nwhat I need to do.
MID_EV11_064_m01_013: We all want to win for you, Cai. Let's make sure\nthat happens.
MID_EV11_064_m01_014: You deserve a happy life with your family. I'll do\nwhatever it takes to get that for you.
MID_EV11_064_m01_015: Same here! I want your wish to come true, Cai.
MID_EV11_064_m01_016: I don't really know how to say this right, but it seems\nlike it should be your turn for good things.
MID_EV11_064_m01_017: I'm so pleased that you are blessed with such good\nfriends, Cai.
MID_EV11_064_m01_018: Hrmmm...
MID_EV11_064_m01_019: You seem lost in thought, Centurio. Something on\nyour mind?
MID_EV11_064_m01_020: And did I see you lugging something out of temple\nstorage this morning?
MID_EV11_064_m01_021: Some old armor maybe?
MID_EV11_064_m01_022: Uh...
MID_EV11_064_m01_023: Cai, there's something you need to know about this\nfight. Your opponent...
MID_EV11_064_m01_024: Centurio, what is it?
MID_EV11_064_m01_025: N-no. I can't say. I will simply pray for your\ngood fortune.
MID_EV11_064_m01_026: Hehehe. Always with the drama, Centurio.
MID_EV11_081_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_081_m01_001: Here we are at last, Bertrand.
MID_EV11_081_m01_002: Indeed. Time to show me that strength you've\nworked so hard to build.
MID_EV11_081_m01_028: 
MID_EV11_081_m01_003: You've changed, Cai! Hardly even look like the\nsame kid.
MID_EV11_081_m01_004: Interesting. So that big brother you always talk about\nis Bertrand?
MID_EV11_081_m01_005: Yep. And, uh—sorry. We got a real bruiser helpin'\nus out too.
MID_EV11_081_m01_006: A real...bruiser?
MID_EV11_081_m01_007: What's with the vulkan out...fit... *gasp*\nWhat's going on?
MID_EV11_081_m01_008: What? But why?
MID_EV11_081_m01_009: This can't be happening! Someone must have made\na mistake!
MID_EV11_081_m01_010: This isn't right... It must be some kind of joke.
MID_EV11_081_m01_011: What are you doing?! Pop, why?!
MID_EV11_081_m01_012: Rrrgh...
MID_EV11_081_m01_013: What is the meaning of this, Centurio?! Why is\nCastor fighting Cai?
MID_EV11_081_m01_014: Someone's making him do this, right? That has to\nbe it.
MID_EV11_081_m01_015: I'm sorry, but no. Castor has chosen this.
MID_EV11_081_m01_016: He had me deliver his old vulkan equipment to him.
MID_EV11_081_m01_017: No...
MID_EV11_081_m01_018: Castor! You must stop this! You can't fight your son!
MID_EV11_081_m01_019: This is real, Cai, and you'd better steel yourself for it\nbecause I won't show you any mercy.
MID_EV11_081_m01_020: But why do I have to fight you, Pop? I don't\nunderstand what's happening.
MID_EV11_081_m01_021: One more fight. It's all I needed for you, me, and\nMom to become a family.
MID_EV11_081_m01_022: Why are you standing in the way?!
MID_EV11_081_m01_023: Did you even think about what this would do\nto Mom?
MID_EV11_081_m01_024: Do you know how much she wants us to be a family?\nStupid old man!
MID_EV11_081_m01_029: 
MID_EV11_081_m01_025: You done?
MID_EV11_081_m01_026: So this is how it is. You want to fight?
MID_EV11_081_m01_027: Fine. I'll give you whatever you want!
MID_EV11_065_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_065_m01_001: So I'm beaten! You've come a long way, Cai.
MID_EV11_065_m01_002: Bertrand...
MID_EV11_065_m01_003: It's alright. I'm glad you're gonna get your wish.
MID_EV11_065_m01_004: Goliath, I'm sorry. Now Bertrand will—
MID_EV11_065_m01_005: He'll be OK. He's got me to help him get out! Besides,\nthe mightier's the rightier—them's the rules.
MID_EV11_065_m01_006: You oughta be happy. You're on top of the world\nright now, little guy!
MID_EV11_065_m01_007: Oh! Right. And Pop...
MID_EV11_065_m01_008: Castor, you idiot! What the hell were you thinking?
MID_EV11_065_m01_009: You...infuriating...idiot!
MID_EV11_065_m01_010: Uh, yeah. Guess I owe you an apology.
MID_EV11_065_m01_011: How can you be such a fool? What if you'd died?
MID_EV11_065_m01_012: Cai worked so hard to save you. You must be the\nmost thickheaded man alive.
MID_EV11_065_m01_013: But...at least you didn't die. We can be grateful\nfor that.
MID_EV11_065_m01_032: <NCA>Ask him why he did it.
MID_EV11_065_m01_014: Pop, what were you thinking?
MID_EV11_065_m01_015: Look. Of course I want us to be a family. But this old\nbody of mine isn't long for this world.
MID_EV11_065_m01_016: I took Bertrand's story to heart, and I started thinking\nabout the time I've got left.
MID_EV11_065_m01_017: With the little bit of life I have, I really oughta help\na good guy like him, right?
MID_EV11_065_m01_018: He has a complicated history of his own, but the\nfuture should be for men like him, not me.
MID_EV11_065_m01_019: But if Bertrand won, you'd have been executed.
MID_EV11_065_m01_020: There's more to it, Cai. I also wanted to put your\nskills to a real test.
MID_EV11_065_m01_021: You fought me head-on and won, and it was no\neasy victory.
MID_EV11_065_m01_022: This will sound strange, but I was so proud of you\nwhen you beat me.
MID_EV11_065_m01_023: My son learned everything I taught him, and then \nsome. I've done everything I need to do in this world.
MID_EV11_065_m01_024: What?! You idiot! You can't just decide that you're\ndone with your life!
MID_EV11_065_m01_025: Didn't you even think about how important that life\nis to Mom?
MID_EV11_065_m01_026: She's worried about how little time we'll have\ntogether too, but she didn't give up on you.
MID_EV11_065_m01_027: She wants to spend whatever time we have making\ngood memories together.
MID_EV11_065_m01_028: Are you...crying?
MID_EV11_065_m01_029: You just don't get it. You really are an idiot, you\nknow that?
MID_EV11_065_m01_030: Long after we've put Dagsion behind us, you'll be\nhearing me tell you that every day.
MID_EV11_065_m01_031: Hahaha. Every day? Really?
MID_EV11_066_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_066_m01_001: First of all, I must extend to you my heartfelt\ncongratulations on your victory in the Heroic Games. 
MID_EV11_066_m01_074: To commemorate your triumph, as Divine Sovereign,\nI bestow upon you the title Flame Lord of Dagda.
MID_EV11_066_m01_075: For your stunning power, you will be known by one\nand all as Hell's-Eye.
MID_EV11_066_m01_076: That's very generous. And I guess this is the part\nwhere we talk about my prize for winning.
MID_EV11_066_m01_002: Before we get into it, can we clear the room? I don't\nreally want a lot of people hearing this.
MID_EV11_066_m01_003: I trust those present. You needn't worry about any\nsecrets being exposed.
MID_EV11_066_m01_004: In that case...
MID_EV11_066_m01_005: Hello, Father. It's been a while, hasn't it? I'm relieved\nto see you doing so well.
MID_EV11_066_m01_006: Aurora? What's the meaning of this?
MID_EV11_066_m01_007: My presence here is perfectly reasonable. After all,\nCai is unquestionably my son.
MID_EV11_066_m01_008: And didn't you promise to grant an audience to\nhis mother?
MID_EV11_066_m01_009: I'm here to claim our prize, Father.
MID_EV11_066_m01_010: What?!
MID_EV11_066_m01_011: Aah! Uh... Huh?!
MID_EV11_066_m01_012: Everyone. I'm sorry, but...leave us.
MID_EV11_066_m01_014: Father, you have some notion that I might not be\nyour child, don't you?
MID_EV11_066_m01_015: Ridiculous. Who told you such nonsense?
MID_EV11_066_m01_016: No one. It's merely become clearer and clearer to me\nas I've thought it through.
MID_EV11_066_m01_019: Ahh...
MID_EV11_066_m01_023: In my memories, Mother is beautiful and kind. And\nyet I recall a loneliness to her as well.
MID_EV11_066_m01_077: At the time, I couldn't imagine why she would feel\nthat way.
MID_EV11_066_m01_024: I remember thinking that it was her experience in\nDamascar that changed her.
MID_EV11_066_m01_026: I see it much more clearly now. Mother was in pain.
MID_EV11_066_m01_027: She agonized over the guilt of betraying you, even\nthough she did it to save so many lives.
MID_EV11_066_m01_028: Around the time of the disappearances in your\ntemple, many rumors swirled around the city.
MID_EV11_066_m01_078: Among them was the suggestion that you were not\nmy child.
MID_EV11_066_m01_031: As you'd become the object of public curiosity,\nI sought to quiet the rumors by hiding you away.
MID_EV11_066_m01_032: And then I received eyewitness testimony that you\nhad abducted people within your temple.
MID_EV11_066_m01_033: I'm sorry to say I doubted you. I thought perhaps the\nblood of Balor in your veins had corrupted you.
MID_EV11_066_m01_034: Yes, I inherited the accursed blood of Founder Balor,\nwho committed terrible atrocities.
MID_EV11_066_m01_035: Perhaps his line should've died out long ago, but\nhere we are.
MID_EV11_066_m01_038: My grandfather's curse doesn't determine who I am,\njust as you are not the sum of your own lineage.
MID_EV11_066_m01_039: Father, you took one of Balor's daughters as\nyour wife.
MID_EV11_066_m01_040: You wanted to be together, even if it put the whole\nworld in disarray, didn't you?
MID_EV11_066_m01_041: You had no qualms about defying the progenitor god.
MID_EV11_066_m01_042: Did you not take Mother away from that island?
MID_EV11_066_m01_043: Yes, she may have seemed distant. But I have no\ndoubt that she believed in you.
MID_EV11_066_m01_044: Why couldn't you have done more to help her?
MID_EV11_066_m01_045: Think of how much happier she would have been.
MID_EV11_066_m01_047: You say I had "no qualms" about defiance. I suppose\nI'd forgotten my former mindset.
MID_EV11_066_m01_048: What I do know is that you still manage to call \nme Father, somehow.
MID_EV11_066_m01_079: My blood doesn't matter. I am still your daughter.
MID_EV11_066_m01_080: For so long, I thought I'd never forgive you because\nyou couldn't protect my mother.
MID_EV11_066_m01_081: But that was because I'd have lost my mind if I'd\nlooked at the situation any other way.
MID_EV11_066_m01_082: If I'm being honest, my heart was weak.
MID_EV11_066_m01_083: But I understand now, Father.
MID_EV11_066_m01_049: The love you've shown me is so precious.
MID_EV11_066_m01_050: And I will always be your daughter!
MID_EV11_066_m01_054: Ahem... You know, the more I listen to you two, the\nmore alike you seem.
MID_EV11_066_m01_055: Both of you told me that a long lifespan can feel like\na cage. That's the word you both used. Cage.
MID_EV11_066_m01_056: That's pretty amazing to me. Makes me feel like\nyou're family.
MID_EV11_066_m01_057: Oh...
MID_EV11_066_m01_058: Father, I want to thank you for everything you've\ndone so far.
MID_EV11_066_m01_059: I will never forget the love you've shown me.
MID_EV11_066_m01_061: But I'm about to defy you so I can follow my heart.
MID_EV11_066_m01_062: I'm leaving my temple. I'm taking my son and my\nhusband, who is currently in your dungeon.
MID_EV11_066_m01_063: We will not inconvenience you, but I will abandon\nmy name and my station to live quietly as mortals do.
MID_EV11_066_m01_064: And yes, I know those closest to me will die ahead\nof me.
MID_EV11_066_m01_065: But I want to live life to the fullest, making memories\nwith them. Cai and his friends taught me that. 
MID_EV11_066_m01_066: I understand, and I grant you your desire. Live freely,\nthe way mortals live.
MID_EV11_066_m01_067: And if you'll allow it, I would like to visit your home\none day.
MID_EV11_066_m01_068: I'll have someone I'll want you to meet too, although\nthat will have to wait for a while.
MID_EV11_066_m01_069: Oh my! Someone you'll want me to meet? A new\npartner, perhaps?
MID_EV11_066_m01_070: Hahaha. Yes, perhaps. You might be surprised.
MID_EV11_066_m01_071: Cai, I owe you my gratitude. Because of you, I've\nrenewed my connection with my beloved Aurora.
MID_EV11_066_m01_072: As Aurora's son... Well, that makes you my grandson,\ndoesn't it? Haha. Family is a delight.
MID_EV11_066_m01_073: Cai, thank you, truly. You've saved me, it seems, just\nas you saved Aurora.
MID_NR11_01_m01: <SH>
MID_NR11_01_m01_001: With Cai's wish granted, Castor was duly freed.
MID_NR11_01_m01_002: The family rented a house in the outskirts of the\nimperial capital while Castor convalesced.
MID_NR11_01_m01_003: Aurora abdicated her status as a goddess and took\nthe name Laura, living as a mortal with her family.
MID_NR11_01_m01_004: The peaceful, happy life they had all wished for\nfinally began.
MID_NR11_01_m01_005: —Saint Cichol, "Fearsome Warriors,"\nPart 1, Chapter 12
MID_EV11_067_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_067_m01_001: Mom, what's that sound? Is the pot boiling over?!
MID_EV11_067_m01_002: Way to be observant, Cai! But what do I do?
MID_EV11_067_m01_003: Stay calm, carefully pull a few logs out of the oven,\nand it'll be fine. Just gotta reduce the heat a little.
MID_EV11_067_m01_004: Not like that! Don't use your hands! Use tongs!
MID_EV11_067_m01_005: You two alright? Maybe I oughta help too.
MID_EV11_067_m01_006: No! You're supposed to be resting!
MID_EV11_067_m01_007: Yeah, you're finally doing better. Last thing you need\nis to rush around cleaning up after us.
MID_EV11_067_m01_008: Fine, fine. I'm no match for you two anyway.
MID_EV11_067_m01_009: Firewood's chopped. I'll leave some here for you.
MID_EV11_067_m01_010: But, um, you cut too deep on the shem yam. It kind\nof wastes a lot when you peel so much off.
MID_EV11_067_m01_011: Oh, sure. It's easy to criticize, but it's hard using the\nknife. It's not really made for peeling, is it?
MID_EV11_067_m01_012: Well, there you go. You're not supposed to peel a\nshem yam with a knife.
MID_EV11_067_m01_013: You start by making a cut in it. Then you quickly\ngrill the outside, and the skin practically falls off.
MID_EV11_067_m01_015: Mercy. What would I do without you teaching me\neverything? I'm a terrible mother.
MID_EV11_067_m01_016: Nah, everyone needs to learn this stuff, Mom. You'll\nfigure it out, one thing at a time.
MID_EV11_067_m01_019: Hey, when Pop's feeling better, we should all travel\naround Dagda together.
MID_EV11_067_m01_020: There's a bunch of places I wanna show you. You've\nhardly ever been out of the temple, right?
MID_EV11_067_m01_021: You're like one of those over-protected kids, huh?\nGrandpa Solel was kinda strict.
MID_EV11_067_m01_022: Hehe. You're probably right about that. I'm looking\nforward to traveling with my boys.
MID_EV11_067_m01_023: For now, can we focus on the food? Everyone'll be\nhere soon. Is everything gonna be ready?
MID_EV11_067_m01_024: It's nice that Ultand and Centurio are close by so we\ncan see them pretty often.
MID_EV11_067_m01_025: But it's been a while since we saw Tialla and Peter\nnow that they're back in Ribeira.
MID_EV11_067_m01_026: Mom, you watch the oven. I'll fetch some water.
MID_EV11_067_m01_027: I'll do my best to...not burn the house down.
MID_EV11_067_m01_028: This is great, being together this way.
MID_EV11_067_m01_029: Better get that water.
MID_EV11_068_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_068_m01_001: Lord Solel, you look very pleased. What's happened?
MID_EV11_068_m01_002: I spoke with Aurora for the first time in a long while.\nHaha. She slapped me, with great force.
MID_EV11_068_m01_003: Is that so?
MID_EV11_068_m01_004: I've been terrible to that girl, but she still has the\nkindness to call me Father, even now.
MID_EV11_068_m01_005: Honestly, that touched me. It made me very happy.
MID_EV11_068_m01_006: Perhaps it was because so much time passed since I\nlast saw her. She's become a truly splendid person.
MID_EV11_068_m01_007: I see.
MID_EV11_068_m01_008: Don't you want to speak with her too? I think she\nwould like that very much.
MID_EV11_068_m01_009: I'm so sorry. I just can't grasp any feeling for Aurora\nas a daughter, no matter how hard I try.
MID_EV11_068_m01_010: I become so very uneasy when I think of her.\nIt's such an unsettling feeling.
MID_EV11_068_m01_011: I just... I just need a little more time.
MID_EV11_068_m01_012: Hmm.
MID_EV11_068_m01_013: Of course. I'm sorry. I don't mean to push you into\nsomething you can't handle.
MID_EV11_068_m01_014: Please, spend the rest of the day relaxing.
MID_EV11_068_m01_015: I'm sorry I made you uneasy, Yu Phas.